# 식당 아저씨: laughs a lot, and everything comes back to food. (format: js/core/villagers.js)

=== person ajeossi
at morning sikdang 50 52
at afternoon sikdang 50 52
at evening sikdang 50 52
greet aj_hi
chat 0 aj_special
chat 0 aj_gramps
chat 0 aj_order
bye aj_bye

=== scene aj_hi
ajeossi[happy]: {어서 오세요}! {먹었어요}?
(He is already reaching for a plate.)

=== scene aj_special
ajeossi[happy]: {오늘}{은|은/는} {떡볶이}{가|이/가} {맛있어요}!
(He lifts the lid off a pan. It is very, very red.)
* {떡볶이} {주세요}! -> aj_special_a
* {매워요}...? -> aj_special_b

=== scene aj_special_a
ajeossi[happy]: 하하! {네}! {여기} {있어요}.
(A plate lands in front of you before you finish the sentence.)
! rel ajeossi +1

=== scene aj_special_b
ajeossi: {매워요}? {아니요}, {아니요}. {안} {매워요}!
(It is extremely spicy. He watches you find that out, delighted.)

=== scene aj_gramps
ajeossi[worried]: {할아버지} {봤어요}? {오늘} {안} {왔어요}.
(He glances at the empty stool by the window.)
* {강}{에} {있어요}. -> aj_gramps_a
* {몰라요}. -> aj_gramps_b

=== scene aj_gramps_a
ajeossi[happy]: 아, {강}! {낚시}! 하하. {고마워요}.
(He mimes casting a line and shakes his head, smiling.)
! rel ajeossi +1

=== scene aj_gramps_b
ajeossi: {네}... {이상해요}.
(He wipes the same spot on the counter three times.)

=== scene aj_order
ajeossi: {뭐} {먹어요}?
(He taps the menu on the wall with his cloth.)
@build Order something.
tiles: {라면} | {비빔밥} | {김밥} | {물} | {주세요}
answer: {라면} | {주세요} -> aj_order_a
answer: {비빔밥} | {주세요} -> aj_order_a
answer: {김밥} | {주세요} -> aj_order_a
answer: {물} | {주세요} -> aj_order_w
miss -> aj_order_no

=== scene aj_order_no
ajeossi[surprised]: {네}?
~ The food first, then 주세요.
<- aj_order.2

=== scene aj_order_a
ajeossi[happy]: {네}! {맛있어요}! 하하.
(He says it is delicious before you have tasted it. He is right.)
! rel ajeossi +1

=== scene aj_order_w
ajeossi: {물}? {네}... {여기} {있어요}.
(He looks a little hurt. Water, in his restaurant.)

=== scene aj_bye
ajeossi: {바빠요}! 하하. {내일} {오세요}!
(The lunch crowd is coming in. Tomorrow.)
